        "heading": "Auspicious Interpretations — When Flying Dreams Forecast Success",
        "body": "Flying freely and high through the open sky is ranked among the most auspicious dream categories in Korean traditional interpretation (꿈해몽). The core principle is straightforward: the higher and more freely you fly, the greater the fortune being foretold.\n\n### Flying high — the strongest success signal\n\nSoaring above the clouds or reaching the stars signals extraordinary achievement ahead — exam success, a promotion arriving sooner than expected, unexpected financial gain, or a business breakthrough. A safe, smooth landing within the dream is read as confirmation: whatever goal you have been pursuing is all but certain to be achieved. The dream is not vague encouragement; it is treated as specific timing intelligence.\n\n### Sprouting wings or transforming into a bird\n\nDreaming that wings grow from under your arms and you rise skyward signals recognition by those in power — a promotion, appointment, or social elevation you may not have anticipated. Transforming into a bird carries similar weight. Flying as a crane (학) specifically foretells honor and prestige; flying as an eagle predicts commanding leadership over many people.\n\n### Riding a dragon or drifting on clouds\n\nFlying on a dragon's back is one of the most powerful auspicious omens in the entire canon — it foretells major public recognition, electoral victory, or transformative success in business. Drifting serenely on clouds is gentler in tone but still auspicious, representing the gradual opening of new opportunities and advancement.\n\n### Flying in or piloting an airplane\n\nAirplane dreams translate the ancient symbol into modern terms. Boarding a plane signals freedom and incoming opportunity; piloting the aircraft yourself is the stronger reading — it foretells self-directed, autonomously achieved success, and a period when your creative capacity will be fully expressed.",
